# Adding Basketball Training Programs

This project extracts workout data from CoachIQ HTML files and builds a mobile-friendly MkDocs Material site deployed to GitHub Pages at https://ronyguga.github.io/bskt_bym/

## Two Program Types

### 1. Weekly Programs (multiple weeks with daily workouts)
Files named `wXX.dY.html`, may include `wXX.film.NAME.html` or `wXX.m.html` (mobility).

```bash
python extract_program.py "<FolderName>" --program-name "Display Name"
```

Outputs `<FolderName>/workouts/weekXX.md` + `index.md`.

### 2. Simple Programs (numbered video files, no weekly structure)
Files named `01 - Title.html`, `02 - Title.html`, etc.

```bash
python extract_simple.py "<FolderName>" --program-name "Display Name"
```

Outputs `<FolderName>/workouts/index.md` with a video table. If any files contain Slide/Block workout data (e.g. `DayX.html`), those are rendered as exercise tables below.

## After Extraction, Update 4 Files

1. **`prepare_docs.py`** — Add to `PROGRAMS` dict: `"slug": ROOT / "FolderName" / "workouts"`
2. **`mkdocs.yml`** — Add nav entry under `nav:`. Weekly programs need per-week entries; simple programs need just `- Name: slug/index.md`
3. **`docs/index.md`** — Add a row to the programs table
4. **`.gitignore`** — Add `docs/slug/`

## Build & Deploy

```bash
python prepare_docs.py    # copies workout .md files into docs/
mkdocs build              # builds the static site
git add . && git commit -m "Add <program name>" && git push
```

GitHub Actions auto-deploys on push to `main`.

## Key Technical Details
- HTML files use Next.js RSC format; data is extracted via regex from `self.__next_f.push()` calls
- S3 `.mov` URLs are converted to CloudFront `.mp4` playable links
- The `BLOCK_RE` regex handles escaped quotes in content fields
- Film study files use `asset_details` Media structure (no Slides/Blocks)
- Info-only slides (like "flex day" instructions) render as blockquotes
